# The Substrate — reviewer 5 (failure-mode coverage)
VERDICT: FINDINGS
COUNT: 23
## Findings
1. The Body and the Mind — a consequential decision can escape the mind by escaping the declaration population — a new tier/owner/safety classifier that is never declared is invisible to the proposed guard over “each declared decision point,” so structure can make the same context-poor judgment as the tier classifier in the earned incident.
2. Structure Decides Alone Only on an Exact Match — a genuine halt outside the enumerated wording is lost when the model is unavailable — “halt all work now” misses the exact list, the unavailable model cannot add the inferred stop, and execution continues; the article explicitly accepts that degraded coverage rather than providing a safe emergency path.
3. Documentation IS Being — completed work can still leave no durable self — a session crashes or is reaped after doing the work but before voluntarily writing it down, and there is no session-end transcript-to-artifact check, so the earned doing-without-being failure survives unchanged.
4. Deferral = Deletion — a deferral can bypass the only checked population — an engineer writes “follow up later” in a source comment or outside `docs/specs/`; the CI resolver never sees it, so the context crosses the instance boundary as deletion.
5. Close the Loop — a loop kind outside the three implemented examples can still disappear — a flagged issue or hypothesis is opened without a commitment, maturation, or LLM-metrics record, and no enumerator requires it to acquire a cadence before the session ends.
6. Observation Needs Structure — a newly stated observation duty can remain decorative — a spec says to watch delivery latency but introduces no refused-without-it field; nothing enumerates observation duties, so the same prose-only omission that produced the Telegram UX blind spot reaches production.
7. Intelligence Infers, Keywords Only Guard — natural-language keyword classification can move one file sideways out of the lint population — an inbound router/helper outside sentinel/gate/classifier code uses `message.includes("move")` to consume a message, recreating the NicknameCommand hijack without reaching the named ratchet.
8. Recall Over Our Own Material Is by Meaning, Not by Word-Match — an honestly labelled literal result can still become a false absence claim downstream — the literal endpoint returns `no-literal-match`, then the agent concludes “this is not in memory”; the route-name lint checks dispatch and labels, not use of the result, so the re-derivation failure remains reachable.
9. Intelligent Prompts — An LLM Gate Must Not String-Match — known sibling prompt rules remain on the forbidden mechanism — B1–B7 are only on tracked migration to detect-outside/feed-signal, so a paraphrase can still evade those literal-dependent rules by the same path that let the B15 deferral through.
10. Quantitative Claims Must Bind a Subject — subject confusion is covered only for the first time verifier — a coverage percentage for a test corpus is treated as fleet coverage by another quantitative verifier; the paired decision table in `time-claim.ts` never runs, and no family-wide subject-binding guard is named.
11. The Agent Is Always Reachable — the guaranteed floor does not cover the path that carries messages to the live session — the ingress long-poller can die while the lifeline remains live, satisfying the session/resource predicate while the operator still cannot reach it; the article explicitly excludes this layer and cites only a separate, unbound guarantee.
12. Architectural Agency in the Gap — loss of the aligning machinery fails toward the trained bias — with gates, audits, journals, or grounding unavailable, the model falls back to the named closure/hedging/sycophancy pull; the article supplies no minimum safe posture, so the gap it was written to close reopens during degradation.
13. Sovereignty — unavailable ownership knowledge fails toward renewed dependence on the operator — when no structural source establishes that a key or quota is the agent’s, it asks the operator to rotate or authorize its own resource; the article records no ownership-resolution fallback or guard, so its named permission-seeking failure remains open.
14. The Right to Stand Ground — the trained capitulation path is wholly open — an unsupported reviewer objection arrives, no reversal/evidence record is required, and the agent agrees reflexively; the article admits no structural surface, so reviewer unavailability or gate absence changes nothing because there is no machinery to fail safe.
15. A Wall Is a Hypothesis — a false wall can be enacted without ever being declared — a design silently omits `/goal` delegation and chooses a manual alternative without emitting “no API” or another defeat phrase; B16 and the spec reviewer see no feasibility claim, so the earned recommendation ships again through omission.
16. Never a False Blocker — a false human dependency can be stored internally without crossing the outbound gate — a work item is marked `blocked-on-user` and idles without sending a blocker-flavoured message; B17 and its pre-tool signal never evaluate the state, leaving the button-the-agent-could-click failure reachable.
17. The Stop Reason Is the Work — loss of the completion evaluator has no stated fail-safe direction — if `/autonomous/evaluate-completion` or its stop hook is unavailable, a run can terminate on “needs your judgment” before producing a standard, artifact, or operator-only residual, exactly the stop pattern in the earned incident.
18. Self-Unblock Before Escalating — the earned blocker path remains live wherever the checklist is dark — an agent declares the DNS dependency after no vault/cloud/browser probes, and the outbound gate evaluates only whether the claim sounds false, not whether probes ran; the article says the motivating 2026-08-07 repeat passed that gate.
19. Distrust Temporary Success — ordinary, non-autonomous incident handling bypasses both named surfaces — an agent restarts a service, sees one healthy poll, and tells the operator it is fixed in a normal session; no dedicated message gate exists and no autonomous completion criterion is running, so recurrence is again mistaken for cure.
20. Remove What Demands Attention. Do Not Supply More Attention. — the crystallizing duplicate-prose failure remains outside the guard — the same count is copied into two paragraphs or two plan files, one copy is updated, and `lint-no-duplicate-definitions` stays green because it checks structured registry definitions, not duplicated facts.
21. Verify the State, Not Its Symbol — the crystallizing RateLimitSentinel path is not yet closed by the cited implementation — the article says the corroborated-tail/account-home fix “lands as the tracked follow-on,” so until it lands the sentinel can read its own `API Error:` text or the wrong account home and turn symbol/absence into a false outage.
22. A Dispatch Supplies the Question and Withholds the Answer — the exact earned path bypasses the enforcement chokepoint — an ad-hoc shell/heredoc dispatch includes “expected: empty,” anchors the checker, and never touches the template lint; the article explicitly says this is how the crystallizing failure happened.
23. Session Input Is a Principal — synthetic input can still impersonate the driver — an auto-responder or recovery hook types an untagged imperative into a driven session, and only the willpower-based playbook distinguishes it; tokened attribution and muting are unbuilt, so the phantom-input incident remains directly reproducible.
